.Dd October 19, 2026
.Dt VOP_CREATE 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm VOP_CREATE ,
.Nm VOP_MKNOD ,
.Nm VOP_MKDIR ,
.Nm VOP_TMPFILE ,
.Nm VOP_SYMLINK
.Nd create a file, socket, fifo, device, directory or symlink
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/param.h
.In sys/vnode.h
.In sys/namei.h
.Ft int
.Fn VOP_CREATE "struct vnode *dvp" "struct vnode **vpp" "struct componentname *cnp" "struct vattr *vap"
.Ft int
.Fn VOP_TMPFILE "struct vnode *dvp" "struct vnode **vpp" "struct componentname *cnp" "struct vattr *vap"
.Ft int
.Fn VOP_MKNOD "struct vnode *dvp" "struct vnode **vpp" "struct componentname *cnp" "struct vattr *vap"
.Ft int
.Fn VOP_MKDIR "struct vnode *dvp" "struct vnode **vpp" "struct componentname *cnp" "struct vattr *vap"
.Ft int
.Fn VOP_SYMLINK "struct vnode *dvp" "struct vnode **vpp" "struct componentname *cnp" "struct vattr *vap" "const char *target"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These entry points create a new file, socket, fifo, device, directory or symlink
in a given directory.
.Pp
The arguments are:
.Bl -tag -width target
.It Fa dvp
The locked vnode of the directory.
.It Fa vpp
The address of a variable where the resulting locked vnode should be stored.
.It Fa cnp
The pathname component created.
.It Fa vap
The attributes that the new object should be created with.
.It Fa target
The pathname of the target of the symlink.
.El
.Pp
These entry points are called after
.Xr VOP_LOOKUP 9
when an object is being created.
.Pp
.Fn VOP_TMPFILE
creates a regular file with a link count of zero and no directory entry.
The directory entries and its modification time do not change.
The caller checks write and search access and the MAC create policy,
and holds a file system write reference.
The component name is empty, and
.Fa vap->va_type
is
.Dv VREG .
The
.Dv VA_EXCLUSIVE
flag in
.Fa vap->va_vaflags
prevents the new file from acquiring a name.
Otherwise the file system permits a link to the unnamed file once.
After that link and any other names are removed,
the file cannot be linked again.
On failure,
.Fa *vpp
is
.Dv NULL .
.Sh LOCKS
The directory,
.Fa dvp
will be locked on entry and must remain locked on return.
If the call is successful, the new object will be returned locked.
For
.Fn VOP_TMPFILE ,
both locks are exclusive.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
If successful, the vnode for the new object is placed in
.Fa *vpp
and zero is returned.
Otherwise, an appropriate error is returned.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er ENOSPC
The file system is full.
.It Bq Er EDQUOT
The user's file system space or inode quota would be exceeded.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
The file system does not support
.Fn VOP_TMPFILE .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vnode 9 ,
.Xr VOP_LOOKUP 9
.Sh STANDARDS
.Fn VOP_TMPFILE
is specific to the freebsd-android-native fork.
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn VOP_TMPFILE
first appeared in the freebsd-android-native fork of
.Fx 15.1 .
.Pp
The function
.Nm
appeared in
.Bx 4.3 .
.Sh AUTHORS
This manual page was written by
.An Doug Rabson .
